## 1. System Overview

{{ project_name }} is a Domain Control Unit (DCU) serving as a zone gateway and body domain
controller. Built on NXP {{ mcu }} with {{ asil_label }} safety level, it routes CAN, LIN,
and Ethernet (SOME/IP) traffic between vehicle domains.

### Communication Matrix

| Interface | Type | Speed | Purpose |
|:----------|:-----|:-----:|:--------|
| CAN0 | CAN FD | 2 Mbps | Body CAN (doors, lights, wipers) |
| CAN1 | CAN FD | 2 Mbps | Chassis CAN (brake, steering) |
| CAN2 | CAN 2.0 | 500 kbps | Diagnostic CAN |
| Eth0 | 100BASE-T1 | 100 Mbps | SOME/IP to central gateway |
| LIN0 | LIN 2.1 | 19.2 kbps | Local zone sensors/actuators |

---

## 2. Gateway Routing

### DCU-GW-001: CAN-to-CAN Routing
- The system SHALL route CAN messages between CAN0, CAN1, and CAN2 based on routing table
- The system SHALL support up to 256 route entries with configurable filter masks
- The system SHALL forward messages within 1 ms of reception
- The system SHALL support routing enable/disable per entry during runtime

### DCU-GW-002: Signal Gateway
- The system SHALL extract individual signals from CAN frames and repack into different frames
- The system SHALL support signal conversion (endianness, scaling, offset)
- The system SHALL validate signal range before forwarding

### DCU-GW-003: CAN-to-Ethernet Gateway
- The system SHALL encapsulate CAN messages into SOME/IP-SD events
- The system SHALL support up to 50 SOME/IP service instances
- The system SHALL serialize CAN signal groups into PDUs at 10 ms intervals

---

## 3. Ethernet Communication (SOME/IP)

### DCU-ETH-001: SOME/IP Service Discovery
- The system SHALL implement SOME/IP-SD per AUTOSAR PRS protocol
- The system SHALL support Offer/Subscribe/StopOffer entry types
- The system SHALL send FindService entries on network activation

### DCU-ETH-002: SOME/IP Event Communication
- The system SHALL publish vehicle state events via SOME/IP notifications
- The system SHALL support Event Groups for selective subscription
- The system SHALL respect initial delay and repetition phase per AR 4.x

### DCU-ETH-003: DoIP (Diagnostic over IP)
- The system SHALL support DoIP for UDS diagnostic routing via Ethernet
- The system SHALL handle logical address assignment and routing activation
- The system SHALL support up to 16 concurrent diagnostic sessions

---

## 4. Diagnostic Functions

### DCU-DIAG-001: Diagnostic Gateway
- The system SHALL support UDS routing between diagnostic requestor and target ECUs
- The system SHALL maintain a diagnostic routing table with up to 64 targets
- The system SHALL forward UDS responses back to the diagnostic source

### DCU-DIAG-002: Event Memory
- The system SHALL store Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) per ISO 14229-1
- The system SHALL support up to 256 DTC entries with freeze frame data
- The system SHALL support DTC status mask operations

---

## 5. Safety Requirements

### DCU-SAF-001: Gateway Safety (ASIL B)
- The system SHALL monitor critical path routing with a watchdog (100 ms timeout)
- The system SHALL verify CAN routing data consistency via CRC on routing table
- The system SHALL detect routing table corruption and enter safe state

### DCU-SAF-002: Communication Isolation
- The system SHALL isolate safety-critical CAN channels from non-critical channels
- The system SHALL prevent bus-off on one channel from affecting other channels
- The system SHALL protect routing table RAM using E2E profile 1

### DCU-SAF-003: Secure Boot
- The system SHALL verify firmware integrity via HSM crypto block before execution
- The system SHALL authenticate diagnostic session requests via secure access (0x27)
- The system SHALL support secure on-board communication (SecOC)

---

## 6. Acceptance Scenarios

### Scenario: CAN Routing
- GIVEN the gateway is running with 50 route entries
- WHEN a CAN message arrives on CAN0 with matching ID
- THEN the message SHALL be forwarded to CAN1 within 1 ms
- AND the forwarding counter SHALL increment

### Scenario: SOME/IP Event
- GIVEN a SOME/IP service is offered
- WHEN a client subscribes to an event group
- THEN the gateway SHALL start publishing events at the configured interval
- AND correct SOME/IP header SHALL be present

### Scenario: Diagnostic Routing
- GIVEN the diagnostic gateway is active
- WHEN a UDS request arrives on CAN2 for target ECU
- THEN the request SHALL be forwarded to the target via CAN1
- AND the response SHALL be routed back to CAN2
